Hence each point (R\in \mathcal{S}) not collinear with (P,Q) naturally determines a point
[
\Phi(R) ;=; \bigl(,\alpha(R),,k(R)\bigr)
;;\in;; (0,\pi)\times (0,\infty).
]
Let us call (\Phi(\mathcal{S})\subset (0,\pi)\times (0,\infty)) the “shape‐data set” induced by all (R\in\mathcal{S}).  (If some (R\in \mathcal{S}) is on the line of (P,Q), we simply ignore it, since it cannot form a nondegenerate triangle (PQR).)

